1
00:00:03,802 --> 00:00:05,178
- Miss Kano!
- Hm?

2
00:00:05,762 --> 00:00:07,097
Did she leave already?

3
00:00:07,180 --> 00:00:08,640
Something the matter, ma'am?

4
00:00:08,724 --> 00:00:10,183
She left her phone behind.

5
00:00:11,018 --> 00:00:12,686
I can get it to her.

6
00:00:17,149 --> 00:00:20,986
She lent me her umbrella after all.
It's the least I can do.

7
00:00:23,030 --> 00:00:24,197
<i>Oh!</i>

8
00:00:24,281 --> 00:00:25,615
<i>Found her!</i>

9
00:00:27,701 --> 00:00:28,952
[gasps]

10
00:00:30,287 --> 00:00:32,956
INOMATA

11
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:34,958
[inaudible]

12
00:00:38,044 --> 00:00:40,589
<i>Why is Chinatsu at Taiki's house?</i>

13
00:00:46,845 --> 00:00:48,764
<i>It doesn't matter, I should get home.</i>

14
00:00:49,556 --> 00:00:51,975
<i>I'll ask him tomorrow. Oh.</i>

15
00:01:02,569 --> 00:01:04,905
Hey! Taiki Inomata!

16
00:01:04,988 --> 00:01:06,740
What in the heck is going on here?

17
00:01:06,823 --> 00:01:08,116
[gasps] Hina?

18
00:01:09,326 --> 00:01:12,829
Why is Chinatsu Kano,
Eimei's treasure, at your house,

19
00:01:12,913 --> 00:01:15,207
and why did you, Taiki Inomata,

20
00:01:15,290 --> 00:01:18,627
Eimei's potato face,
just say, "Welcome back" to her?

21
00:01:18,710 --> 00:01:21,129
I demand an explanation!

22
00:01:22,255 --> 00:01:23,340
[Taiki exclaims]

23
00:01:26,176 --> 00:01:27,177
[grunts]

24
00:01:33,141 --> 00:01:35,143
[opening theme song playing]

25
00:01:36,186 --> 00:01:39,439
BLUE BOX

26
00:02:55,599 --> 00:03:01,897
BLUE BOX

27
00:03:02,522 --> 00:03:04,733
EPISODE 6
WISH ME LUCK

28
00:03:04,816 --> 00:03:05,984
[Taiki] The truth is...

29
00:03:06,985 --> 00:03:08,403
TAIKI

30
00:03:08,486 --> 00:03:09,905
CHINATSU

31
00:03:10,572 --> 00:03:11,907
[Hina] I see...

32
00:03:12,532 --> 00:03:15,619
So while Chinatsu's parents
are working overseas, she is...

33
00:03:15,702 --> 00:03:17,662
living together with you and your family.

34
00:03:17,746 --> 00:03:18,747
Got it.

35
00:03:18,830 --> 00:03:23,043
Sorry. You've been so supportive
with me having a crush on her,

36
00:03:23,126 --> 00:03:24,419
and I kept this from you.

37
00:03:25,170 --> 00:03:27,464
I'm pretty shocked if I'm being honest.

38
00:03:28,256 --> 00:03:30,425
To find out how little you trust me.

39
00:03:31,927 --> 00:03:33,178
I'm sorry.

40
00:03:33,678 --> 00:03:36,139
And here I was thinking we were besties.

41
00:03:37,265 --> 00:03:40,435
I thought you were totally nuts
going after Chinatsu.

42
00:03:40,518 --> 00:03:41,686
{\an8}JUMP

43
00:03:41,770 --> 00:03:43,647
{\an8}Turns out, you've been
coming home every day

44
00:03:43,730 --> 00:03:45,649
{\an8}and spending time alone with her.

45
00:03:45,732 --> 00:03:47,192
{\an8}[Taiki grunts]

46
00:03:48,401 --> 00:03:49,945
Whe... where is this going?

47
00:03:50,862 --> 00:03:53,198
Stay still for five hours,
and then I'll forgive you.

48
00:03:53,281 --> 00:03:54,157
What?

49
00:03:54,241 --> 00:03:55,867
I know that it's not just about you,

50
00:03:55,951 --> 00:03:57,911
Chinatsu is wrapped up in this, too,

51
00:03:57,994 --> 00:04:00,205
so I get why you
wouldn't go around telling people.

52
00:04:00,914 --> 00:04:02,749
And I did say that I would help you,

53
00:04:02,832 --> 00:04:04,709
but I admit I've been slacking a bit.

54
00:04:06,795 --> 00:04:09,506
With that said, I'm still pissed at you,
so don't move.

55
00:04:10,131 --> 00:04:12,968
Hina. Thanks a lot.

56
00:04:15,762 --> 00:04:18,890
Also, this is the best you can do
in two months? It's pathetic.

57
00:04:18,974 --> 00:04:19,975
Hey!

58
00:04:27,816 --> 00:04:30,235
There you have it.
They're living together.

59
00:04:30,986 --> 00:04:33,738
I thought they seemed close lately.
Makes sense.

60
00:04:34,447 --> 00:04:36,741
Taiki had a crush on her
before she moved in.

61
00:04:36,825 --> 00:04:39,286
And you don't usually live
with someone of the opposite sex

62
00:04:39,369 --> 00:04:40,787
if you can't stand them.

63
00:04:42,163 --> 00:04:42,998
Which means...

64
00:04:44,249 --> 00:04:45,250
I'm so sorry.

65
00:04:45,333 --> 00:04:46,209
Oh.

66
00:04:50,672 --> 00:04:52,590
<i>What on earth am I doing?</i>

67
00:04:57,345 --> 00:04:59,764
{\an8}EIMEI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

68
00:04:59,848 --> 00:05:02,267
[piano music playing]

69
00:05:12,861 --> 00:05:14,195
[all exclaiming]

70
00:05:15,613 --> 00:05:18,408
[coach] That's our Chono! Sensational!

71
00:05:18,491 --> 00:05:19,784
[Niina] You're so cool.

72
00:05:19,868 --> 00:05:21,036
All in a day's work.

73
00:05:21,119 --> 00:05:23,580
Keep this up, and once you hit nationals,

74
00:05:23,663 --> 00:05:26,541
you could podium, or who knows,
maybe you'll take it all!

75
00:05:26,624 --> 00:05:28,418
Please leave it to me.

76
00:05:28,501 --> 00:05:29,711
I am Hina Chono.

77
00:05:29,794 --> 00:05:31,004
Named for the butterfly,

78
00:05:31,087 --> 00:05:33,298
I'll honor my namesake
and dance beautifully.

79
00:05:33,381 --> 00:05:35,133
You're speaking in riddles.

80
00:05:35,216 --> 00:05:36,301
You never disappoint.

81
00:05:37,052 --> 00:05:39,721
- [girl] Keep it up, Hina.
- [Niina] That was perfect, wasn't it?

82
00:05:39,804 --> 00:05:41,222
- [girl] Totally.
- Hina?

83
00:05:42,348 --> 00:05:44,309
I'm gonna take a little break.

84
00:05:44,392 --> 00:05:46,144
[moody music playing]

85
00:05:52,650 --> 00:05:55,195
<i>I almost missed a step
in that run-through.</i>

86
00:05:55,945 --> 00:05:58,573
<i>And that made my next move a beat behind.</i>

87
00:05:59,365 --> 00:06:01,993
<i>I wasn't focusing enough
on my lines, either.</i>

88
00:06:03,203 --> 00:06:05,080
<i>I gotta practice till its automatic.</i>

89
00:06:06,372 --> 00:06:10,085
<i>Everyone's counting on me.
I can't disappoint them.</i>

90
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:12,921
<i>If I make even a single mistake...</i>

91
00:06:17,425 --> 00:06:20,720
<i>Psh, it's fine.
This is Hina Chono we're talking about!</i>

92
00:06:32,690 --> 00:06:34,609
[exclaims excitedly, grunts]

93
00:06:37,112 --> 00:06:38,613
- Whatcha doing?
- Hina!

94
00:06:38,696 --> 00:06:41,241
Oh. Nothing in particular.

95
00:06:41,324 --> 00:06:42,617
Nothing at all, huh?

96
00:06:43,409 --> 00:06:44,994
Hiding more secrets, are we?

97
00:06:45,078 --> 00:06:48,748
[Taiki] I am not.
One of my toenails dug into my skin.

98
00:06:48,832 --> 00:06:51,126
Ew, I don't wanna know that, stop it!

99
00:06:51,209 --> 00:06:53,253
That's why I didn't tell you before.

100
00:06:53,336 --> 00:06:55,922
[sighs] Well, don't forget the antiseptic.

101
00:06:56,005 --> 00:06:57,006
[exclaims softly]

102
00:06:57,841 --> 00:06:59,134
A wish bracelet?

103
00:06:59,801 --> 00:07:01,761
Do you wear stuff like that?

104
00:07:01,845 --> 00:07:04,264
It's just... [sighs]

105
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:07,767
Chinatsu gave it to me.

106
00:07:08,351 --> 00:07:09,769
Huh?

107
00:07:10,645 --> 00:07:12,397
The two of you must be dating.

108
00:07:12,981 --> 00:07:14,649
- So you're hiding that, too?
- Huh?

109
00:07:14,732 --> 00:07:16,526
This wasn't anything romantic!

110
00:07:17,235 --> 00:07:20,780
We're just two people trying to make it
to nationals. It's that kind of thing.

111
00:07:24,784 --> 00:07:27,036
- That's just beautiful.
- Oh, can it, you jerk!

112
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:31,875
[Hina] <i>"Two people trying
to make it to nationals," huh?</i>

113
00:07:31,958 --> 00:07:33,877
- Keep it up, keep it up!
- Run, run, go!

114
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:37,380
<i>That must mean...
whenever practice gets tough,</i>

115
00:07:37,964 --> 00:07:39,883
<i>they think of the other person,</i>

116
00:07:39,966 --> 00:07:41,134
[sad piano music playing]

117
00:07:41,217 --> 00:07:44,637
<i>and remember that someone else out there
is working as hard as they are.</i>

118
00:07:45,221 --> 00:07:46,222
[Haryu] Taiki!

119
00:07:47,223 --> 00:07:48,391
Focus up!

120
00:07:49,476 --> 00:07:51,686
- Yeah!
- [Hina] <i>And that keeps them going.</i>

121
00:07:52,395 --> 00:07:54,647
<i>I guess that's what they have together.</i>

122
00:07:57,233 --> 00:07:58,401
[music stops]

123
00:08:00,069 --> 00:08:01,154
[gasps]

124
00:08:01,237 --> 00:08:02,697
[sad piano music continues]

125
00:08:03,198 --> 00:08:04,866
<i>Why am I crying?</i>

126
00:08:06,326 --> 00:08:09,662
<i>Prepping for qualifiers
has me all moody. No, thank you.</i>

127
00:08:10,955 --> 00:08:13,666
<i>This is something I need to handle alone.</i>

128
00:08:14,667 --> 00:08:17,754
<i>And being alone... is fine.</i>

129
00:08:55,542 --> 00:08:56,459
[exclaims softly]

130
00:08:57,126 --> 00:08:58,294
[girl 1] She missed it again.

131
00:08:58,378 --> 00:08:59,963
[girl 2] She's done that a lot lately.

132
00:09:00,672 --> 00:09:02,966
Miss Chono. Are you feeling all right?

133
00:09:03,716 --> 00:09:04,759
Oh, boy!

134
00:09:04,842 --> 00:09:07,220
I was up late watching TV
and didn't sleep well.

135
00:09:07,303 --> 00:09:09,472
Sleep is critical, you know.

136
00:09:09,556 --> 00:09:10,473
Sorry about that.

137
00:09:10,557 --> 00:09:13,393
- [Kyo] She seems kind of out of it.
- That's rare for her.

138
00:09:14,310 --> 00:09:15,812
She never misses a beat,

139
00:09:15,895 --> 00:09:17,730
even when she gets nervous.

140
00:09:19,315 --> 00:09:20,483
Hey...

141
00:09:23,111 --> 00:09:25,488
Hold on, that means
she's way off her game.

142
00:09:25,572 --> 00:09:28,116
You better give me 3,000 to keep looking.

143
00:09:28,866 --> 00:09:30,368
Maybe you're right about that,

144
00:09:30,451 --> 00:09:33,121
or maybe she's mad at you about something.

145
00:09:33,204 --> 00:09:34,122
Huh?

146
00:09:34,205 --> 00:09:36,874
[Hina] <i>Yep, yep, yep. That's for the best.</i>

147
00:09:36,958 --> 00:09:41,379
<i>Chinatsu might pull away if she sees Taiki
getting friendly with other girls.</i>

148
00:09:42,130 --> 00:09:44,966
<i>They're not just running into each other
in the hallway,</i>

149
00:09:45,049 --> 00:09:48,136
<i>they live under the same roof.
He doesn't need my help anymore.</i>

150
00:09:49,304 --> 00:09:51,264
<i>I don't wanna kill their vibe, either.</i>

151
00:09:52,223 --> 00:09:55,893
- Let's go visit the potty!
- You don't have to say it so loud.

152
00:09:56,477 --> 00:09:59,439
[Hina] <i>I'll take a step back
from being his friend for now.</i>

153
00:10:00,732 --> 00:10:04,402
I even apologized to her.
Covered in issues of <i>Jump.</i>

154
00:10:04,485 --> 00:10:05,737
What does that mean?

155
00:10:14,662 --> 00:10:17,415
Hina, maybe it's time for a little break?

156
00:10:17,498 --> 00:10:20,084
I know the qualifiers are soon,
but you're killing yourself.

157
00:10:21,961 --> 00:10:23,838
I am 100% okay.

158
00:10:23,921 --> 00:10:25,840
Failing is part of success, you know?

159
00:10:26,466 --> 00:10:28,718
But I'm gonna go take
a mental break, though.

160
00:10:29,469 --> 00:10:30,553
[both exclaim]

161
00:10:31,554 --> 00:10:32,722
{\an8}COLD DRINKS

162
00:10:34,057 --> 00:10:37,060
[Hina] <i>Whatever I say,
I know they're still worried about me.</i>

163
00:10:39,270 --> 00:10:41,522
<i>For someone who's known for her bravado,</i>

164
00:10:41,606 --> 00:10:43,107
<i>this is pathetic.</i>

165
00:10:43,191 --> 00:10:44,734
<i>I need to get it together.</i>

166
00:10:47,820 --> 00:10:49,489
BIOLOGY CLUB

167
00:10:49,572 --> 00:10:51,658
<i>Taiki's stubborn like that boar.</i>

168
00:10:51,741 --> 00:10:53,242
- [vice principal] Miss Chono.
- Hm?

169
00:10:54,243 --> 00:10:55,495
Mr. Vice Principal.

170
00:10:55,578 --> 00:10:58,247
I read your interview in the newspaper!

171
00:10:58,331 --> 00:11:01,292
Goodness, you're not just talented
in rhythmic gymnastics,

172
00:11:01,376 --> 00:11:03,503
you're wonderful in an interview, too!

173
00:11:03,586 --> 00:11:04,754
Thank you very much.

174
00:11:04,837 --> 00:11:07,507
So, tell me,
how is the routine coming along lately?

175
00:11:07,590 --> 00:11:09,634
Qualifiers are coming up, huh?

176
00:11:09,717 --> 00:11:10,760
It's a ten, sir!

177
00:11:10,843 --> 00:11:12,637
Ah. Very good to hear.

178
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:15,515
You're quite the disciplined,
self-starting type, aren't you?

179
00:11:15,598 --> 00:11:19,060
Just what we'd expect
from the daughter of Hirohiko Chono.

180
00:11:19,143 --> 00:11:22,021
- He did represent Japan after all!
- [chuckles]

181
00:11:22,563 --> 00:11:25,066
Might there be a chance
your father would stop by?

182
00:11:25,149 --> 00:11:27,026
We'd love to give him a big Eimei hello.

183
00:11:27,110 --> 00:11:28,611
I'll pass that along!

184
00:11:28,694 --> 00:11:29,779
Please do!

185
00:11:29,862 --> 00:11:32,532
What a fine student we have here!

186
00:11:33,116 --> 00:11:34,242
EXPECTATIONS
4TH PLACE

187
00:11:34,325 --> 00:11:36,994
<i>I have enough weighing
on my shoulders, thank you.</i>

188
00:11:37,078 --> 00:11:38,663
DAD - ARTICLE - CONCERNS - TRAINING

189
00:11:38,746 --> 00:11:41,457
<i>It's not like
I'm that amazing of a person.</i>

190
00:11:42,417 --> 00:11:44,836
<i>I'm just a regular high school first-year.</i>

191
00:11:46,546 --> 00:11:48,172
<i>It's times like these...</i>

192
00:11:49,132 --> 00:11:52,260
<i>I wish I could joke around
with that idiot goody-two-shoes.</i>

193
00:11:52,343 --> 00:11:55,471
<i>The guy who only ever thinks
about the next step,</i>

194
00:11:55,555 --> 00:11:57,432
<i>and keeps moving forward.</i>

195
00:12:00,017 --> 00:12:01,310
Keep it up!

196
00:12:03,229 --> 00:12:04,439
[gasps softly]

197
00:12:13,990 --> 00:12:15,867
[whimpers]

198
00:12:25,042 --> 00:12:26,210
<i>That's right.</i>

199
00:12:27,170 --> 00:12:29,005
<i>I've gotta handle this alone.</i>

200
00:12:35,011 --> 00:12:36,804
[uplifting music playing]

201
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:15,676
Good for her.

202
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:17,220
Looks like our girl is back.

203
00:13:17,803 --> 00:13:19,222
[Hina] All right.

204
00:13:20,806 --> 00:13:22,725
<i>Didn't make one mistake today.</i>

205
00:13:23,684 --> 00:13:25,728
<i>But I'm still feeling a little shaky.</i>

206
00:13:26,604 --> 00:13:28,731
<i>I need to win the prefecturals first,</i>

207
00:13:29,357 --> 00:13:31,150
<i>then get in my best shape
before nationals.</i>

208
00:13:31,234 --> 00:13:34,237
[boy] Oh, hold on. I, uh...
I forgot something. I'll run and grab it.

209
00:13:37,198 --> 00:13:38,241
[Hina gasps]

210
00:13:42,703 --> 00:13:44,372
Oh, I'm sorry! Are you okay?

211
00:13:44,455 --> 00:13:45,623
- What happened?
- Oh, I just...

212
00:13:45,706 --> 00:13:48,626
- [heart beating]
- [Hina breathing shakily]

213
00:13:49,210 --> 00:13:50,378
<i>It hurts...</i>

214
00:13:51,712 --> 00:13:53,214
<i>Did I sprain it?</i>

215
00:13:53,714 --> 00:13:54,966
<i>I can just tape it.</i>

216
00:13:55,716 --> 00:13:58,511
<i>But what if the pain pulls my focus?</i>

217
00:13:59,762 --> 00:14:01,389
No, seriously, are you okay?

218
00:14:02,306 --> 00:14:04,559
[Hina] <i>I'm not
in my best shape to begin with.</i>

219
00:14:05,476 --> 00:14:06,519
<i>What do I do?</i>

220
00:14:07,603 --> 00:14:08,646
<i>What do I do?</i>

221
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:10,690
<i>What do I do?</i>

222
00:14:12,233 --> 00:14:13,693
[Taiki] Can you stand?

223
00:14:13,776 --> 00:14:14,735
[Hina gasps]

224
00:14:18,030 --> 00:14:19,198
Huh?

225
00:14:19,282 --> 00:14:20,908
It's your left ankle?

226
00:14:22,743 --> 00:14:24,996
Come on. Let's have
the nurse check you out.

227
00:14:25,079 --> 00:14:26,956
All good! I don't need help there.

228
00:14:27,582 --> 00:14:29,709
I appreciate it, but I'm okay, you can go.

229
00:14:29,792 --> 00:14:31,127
Oh, okay.

230
00:14:33,254 --> 00:14:36,299
Go on. You don't want Chinatsu
to see us together.

231
00:14:36,382 --> 00:14:37,466
See us?

232
00:14:37,550 --> 00:14:39,886
I'm not thinking about that right now!

233
00:14:41,053 --> 00:14:45,182
You're constantly acting like the world
revolves around the "Great Hina Chono,"

234
00:14:45,266 --> 00:14:47,685
then, when you actually need help,
you overthink it.

235
00:14:47,768 --> 00:14:50,479
- I'll tell the advisor.
- Yeah. Thanks, dude.

236
00:14:51,814 --> 00:14:55,359
It's moments like these
when you should put yourself first.

237
00:14:55,985 --> 00:14:57,194
[gasps softly]

238
00:14:58,696 --> 00:15:01,574
[Taiki] All right, hold on. Up we go.

239
00:15:03,659 --> 00:15:04,619
[Hina] <i>Stop it.</i>

240
00:15:07,163 --> 00:15:07,997
<i>No.</i>

241
00:15:12,877 --> 00:15:15,129
<i>I don't wanna find out what this is.</i>

242
00:15:19,967 --> 00:15:21,886
{\an8}NURSE'S OFFICE

243
00:15:21,969 --> 00:15:24,388
Seems like there's nothing wrong with it.

244
00:15:24,472 --> 00:15:26,891
Nothing... wrong... with it?

245
00:15:27,642 --> 00:15:29,685
You probably knocked it when you fell.

246
00:15:30,394 --> 00:15:33,773
You do have a bruise, but the pain
should subside in a few minutes.

247
00:15:34,607 --> 00:15:38,778
You might be more sensitive to it
because the qualifiers are coming up.

248
00:15:38,861 --> 00:15:41,238
Let's ice it to be on the safe side.

249
00:15:42,490 --> 00:15:44,533
Looks like somebody cried wolf.

250
00:15:44,617 --> 00:15:46,327
It felt real to me!

251
00:15:46,410 --> 00:15:48,788
I've been under
a lot of pressure you know.

252
00:15:48,871 --> 00:15:53,292
[groans] And truth be told,
I haven't been sleeping well, either.

253
00:15:53,376 --> 00:15:54,502
INOMATA COUNSELING

254
00:15:54,585 --> 00:15:56,712
Uh-huh. And when did these symptoms start?

255
00:15:57,630 --> 00:15:59,382
The worst counselor imaginable.

256
00:15:59,966 --> 00:16:01,801
Is that a prompt for your next skit?

257
00:16:02,343 --> 00:16:05,179
I'm gonna stay with you, so lay it on me.

258
00:16:08,265 --> 00:16:10,267
What do they mean
by "the star athlete's daughter"?

259
00:16:10,351 --> 00:16:13,062
I mean, I respect my dad and all,
but I got me here, not him.

260
00:16:13,145 --> 00:16:14,397
People thinking my achievements

261
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:17,400
are 'cause my dad happens to have been
on the national team sucks!

262
00:16:17,483 --> 00:16:20,444
- [Taiki] It doesn't end, does it?
- Our coach just smiles with no advice.

263
00:16:23,990 --> 00:16:27,451
The way things stand, there's one person
who I don't think I can beat.

264
00:16:28,285 --> 00:16:29,704
That's not like you.

265
00:16:29,787 --> 00:16:32,164
You never called any gymnast unbeatable.

266
00:16:33,666 --> 00:16:34,709
[chuckles]

267
00:16:35,292 --> 00:16:38,462
I can't say that I've ever seen someone
in this way before.

268
00:16:39,213 --> 00:16:41,215
The judge is so devoted to her.

269
00:16:41,298 --> 00:16:42,466
What?

270
00:16:42,550 --> 00:16:44,760
You mean she gets scored
based on who she is,

271
00:16:44,844 --> 00:16:46,971
rather than her actual performance?

272
00:16:47,054 --> 00:16:49,056
What can I say, the judge loves her.

273
00:16:49,140 --> 00:16:50,891
Well, that judge can eat my shorts!

274
00:16:50,975 --> 00:16:52,143
I'm pissed off.

275
00:16:52,226 --> 00:16:53,227
Right?

276
00:16:53,310 --> 00:16:54,478
I'm pissed off, too.

277
00:16:57,106 --> 00:16:59,900
But then, she's terribly attractive, so...

278
00:16:59,984 --> 00:17:01,485
I can totally see why.

279
00:17:02,194 --> 00:17:05,448
<i>She catches everyone's attention,
but she's not stuck up about it.</i>

280
00:17:05,531 --> 00:17:07,491
<i>And she works as hard as anyone.</i>

281
00:17:07,575 --> 00:17:09,243
Up against such an opponent,

282
00:17:09,326 --> 00:17:12,496
even I, the Great Chono,
wants to back down and run away.

283
00:17:13,205 --> 00:17:14,999
We both know you'd never run away.

284
00:17:15,082 --> 00:17:16,125
Huh?

285
00:17:16,208 --> 00:17:18,878
You have this kind of
indomitable warrior spirit, you know?

286
00:17:18,961 --> 00:17:20,671
[yelling]

287
00:17:21,255 --> 00:17:22,923
For one, you really hate to lose,

288
00:17:23,007 --> 00:17:24,925
and your pride plays a role in that, too.

289
00:17:25,718 --> 00:17:29,472
But more than anything, you're the kind
who won't back down without a fight.

290
00:17:31,098 --> 00:17:32,558
That is just who you are.

291
00:17:34,018 --> 00:17:35,311
[grunts]

292
00:17:38,397 --> 00:17:39,815
You're pissing me off!

293
00:17:39,899 --> 00:17:41,275
[grunts]

294
00:17:41,358 --> 00:17:44,779
I can think of plenty of scenarios
where the best thing to do is run!

295
00:17:44,862 --> 00:17:46,822
I see the error of my ways, I'm sorry!

296
00:17:48,449 --> 00:17:50,993
Although... you're totally right about me.

297
00:17:52,703 --> 00:17:53,704
[door opens]

298
00:17:53,788 --> 00:17:54,914
That's enough.

299
00:17:54,997 --> 00:17:56,791
It's time to get back to practice.

300
00:17:58,459 --> 00:17:59,710
[Taiki] All right, back we go.

301
00:18:00,503 --> 00:18:02,213
How's your ankle doing?

302
00:18:12,056 --> 00:18:13,474
It doesn't hurt anymore.

303
00:18:17,561 --> 00:18:20,189
Just remember, if you lose,
you have no excuse.

304
00:18:20,272 --> 00:18:21,524
I'm not losing.

305
00:18:25,528 --> 00:18:27,780
- Hey, Taiki.
- Hm?

306
00:18:28,572 --> 00:18:30,533
Do you mind, um...

307
00:18:31,033 --> 00:18:32,243
wishing me luck?

308
00:18:36,038 --> 00:18:37,248
Good luck!

309
00:18:39,625 --> 00:18:42,211
[chuckles]

310
00:18:42,294 --> 00:18:43,629
[happy piano music playing]

311
00:18:45,339 --> 00:18:47,591
Psh, you think I needed that?

312
00:18:47,675 --> 00:18:49,176
[Taiki] You made me say it!

313
00:18:58,352 --> 00:19:00,771
[laughter and applause]

314
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:07,945
Miss Chono, congratulations!

315
00:19:08,028 --> 00:19:11,282
That performance certainly deserved
first place in the qualifiers.

316
00:19:11,907 --> 00:19:13,826
- Great job.
- You killed it!

317
00:19:13,909 --> 00:19:15,035
[Hina chuckles]

318
00:19:15,995 --> 00:19:18,706
You know, I think
I might've been worried over nothing.

319
00:19:18,789 --> 00:19:21,542
Well, good for her.
It all turned out fine.

320
00:19:22,168 --> 00:19:23,794
[Taiki] Yeah, I guess it did.

321
00:19:26,255 --> 00:19:28,674
Whatcha lookin' at, punk? That's ten G's.

322
00:19:28,757 --> 00:19:30,426
You're raising the price?

323
00:19:30,509 --> 00:19:32,428
[Hina laughs] Kidding!

324
00:19:33,470 --> 00:19:35,431
I'm getting more charming by the day!

325
00:19:35,514 --> 00:19:37,558
So make sure that you keep an eye on me.

326
00:19:38,309 --> 00:19:40,561
[vocalizing tune]

327
00:19:40,644 --> 00:19:42,980
Turns out, I was worrying over nothing.

328
00:19:43,606 --> 00:19:44,565
[Kyo] Hm.

329
00:19:45,149 --> 00:19:46,984
<i>As the outside observer in all this,</i>

330
00:19:47,067 --> 00:19:49,820
<i>it feels like it look forever
just to get to this point.</i>

331
00:19:50,738 --> 00:19:53,407
<i>Now it all depends
on Chinatsu's next move.</i>

332
00:19:58,913 --> 00:20:00,289
Good night, sleep well.

333
00:20:00,372 --> 00:20:02,333
- Good night.
- 'Night.

334
00:20:02,416 --> 00:20:03,584
This is really good.

335
00:20:04,501 --> 00:20:07,838
[Taiki] <i>Practice really
tires me out these days.</i>

336
00:20:08,464 --> 00:20:11,217
<i>But with Hina already
earning her spot for nationals,</i>

337
00:20:11,300 --> 00:20:13,385
<i>I need to push harder so I can follow.</i>

338
00:20:14,678 --> 00:20:15,596
[both] Oh.

339
00:20:16,222 --> 00:20:17,306
Heading to bed?

340
00:20:17,389 --> 00:20:19,141
Yeah, how about you?

341
00:20:19,225 --> 00:20:20,434
I'm getting water.

342
00:20:21,185 --> 00:20:22,353
Oh, yeah, got it.

343
00:20:22,937 --> 00:20:26,565
Oh. And by the way,
I saw Hina at the chiropractor today.

344
00:20:26,649 --> 00:20:27,608
What?

345
00:20:28,192 --> 00:20:30,611
Don't tell me that she
ran her mouth at you?

346
00:20:30,694 --> 00:20:34,365
No, she was just thanking me
for the umbrella the other day.

347
00:20:35,032 --> 00:20:37,409
Thank you very much
for your help the other day!

348
00:20:37,493 --> 00:20:40,621
I've started carrying
a foldable umbrella, too, we're twins!

349
00:20:40,704 --> 00:20:42,248
Oh, is that right!

350
00:20:42,831 --> 00:20:44,541
She's amazing, isn't she?

351
00:20:44,625 --> 00:20:47,503
She's a first-year,
and she won prefectural qualifiers.

352
00:20:48,420 --> 00:20:51,340
Although Hina herself
wasn't satisfied with how she did.

353
00:20:51,423 --> 00:20:52,258
Huh?

354
00:20:52,341 --> 00:20:54,969
She said she didn't perform
her routine perfectly.

355
00:20:56,595 --> 00:20:59,223
<i>She was pretty fired up
to iron out all of the kinks,</i>

356
00:20:59,306 --> 00:21:01,267
<i>so she can nail it at nationals.</i>

357
00:21:02,685 --> 00:21:05,271
Hina, a hopeless gymnastics nerd.

358
00:21:05,854 --> 00:21:06,814
[gasps softly]

359
00:21:08,357 --> 00:21:10,901
Ah, okay, right,
I'll be heading to bed, then.

360
00:21:11,735 --> 00:21:13,696
- Sleep well.
- Good night.

361
00:21:14,363 --> 00:21:16,240
[pensive music playing]

362
00:21:17,992 --> 00:21:21,954
He really is a hopeless badminton nerd,
don't ya think, Chinatsu?

363
00:21:29,086 --> 00:21:31,672
<i>The two of them... would be good together.</i>

364
00:21:34,300 --> 00:21:36,260
<i>Hina seems to feel that way about...</i>

365
00:21:37,136 --> 00:21:41,223
<i>That means I'm just getting in the way.</i>

366
00:21:41,307 --> 00:21:43,225
<i>The girl living with the guy.</i>

367
00:21:44,685 --> 00:21:45,769
[gasps softly]

368
00:21:49,273 --> 00:21:50,399
<i>I'm sorry, Hina.</i>

369
00:21:52,568 --> 00:21:54,820
<i>But this is for basketball.</i>

370
00:21:56,196 --> 00:21:59,450
<i>I'm staying his housemate
until I graduate.</i>

371
00:22:02,578 --> 00:22:03,829
[music fades]

372
00:22:05,497 --> 00:22:07,499
[closing theme song playing]
